>>__ load "simpLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `set_looper`

``` hol4
simpLib.set_looper : string * (simpLib.simpset -> tactic) ->
  simpLib.simpset -> simpLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Replaces all the loopers of a simpset with one looper.

`set_looper (name, mk) ss` removes every looper of `ss`, including split
loopers, and adds `mk` as `simpLib.add_looper (name, mk)` does.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val cases = simpLib.++ (boolSimps.bool_ss,simpLib.split_ss);
>>_ val conjunctions = simpLib.set_looper
     ("conj", fn _ => CONJ_TAC) cases;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.add_looper`](#simpLib.add_looper),
[`simpLib.del_looper`](#simpLib.del_looper).
